 "caveats": [
  "Both rules were selected on us100 after seeing the three indices: us100 is the best of three (selection).",
  "noise30 is the published rule with the published parameters (no tuning). Its IS PF is 1.28 on the HH:00/HH:30 grid; with the whole grid shifted by +1/+2/+5/+15/+30 minutes it is 1.175/1.170/1.249/1.231/1.252 (t 2.1-2.9): the data show a +0.4-0.5 bp continuation in the single minute after HH:00/HH:30 when the price is outside the band; the back-test gets it by filling at the first tick of that minute. A live EA should count on PF about 1.2, not 1.28.",
  "ocm4 replaces the literature 5-minute candle (IS PF 1.31, t 3.3): with n=5 about 1.8 bp of the 6.5 bp net edge is earned in the single minute 09:35-09:36 and an entry one minute late gives PF 1.17 (t 1.9). The 4-minute candle enters before that minute; an entry one minute late leaves it unchanged (PF 1.234). Its neighbours n=3 (1.13) and n=5 (1.31) show how noisy the family is: honest PF about 1.2.",
  "ocm4 gross edge per trade halves between 2014-2017 (6.99 bp, t 2.6) and 2018-2021 (3.64 bp, t 0.95); 2015 is a losing year, 2020 flat.",
  "Profits are concentrated: the 10 best days give 53% (noise30) and 47% (ocm4) of the total IS R. Trend-following payoff.",
  "The two sleeves trade the same instrument; daily-R correlation about 0.4 on IS."
 ],
